data.content:
Here are the two files:

**`SortableList.razor`** — the template with Move Up/Down buttons per item, using `@key` for efficient diffing.

**`SortableList.razor.cs`** — the `partial class` code-behind:

- Generic via `TItem`; accepts `Items` (immutable `IReadOnlyList<TItem>`) and an `ItemTemplate` render fragment.
- Copies `Items` into a private `_items` list in `OnParametersSet` — never mutates the caller's collection.
- Swap logic in `MoveUp`/`MoveDown` fires `OnOrderChanged` with a read-only snapshot of the reordered list.

Usage matches your example:

```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private List<TaskItem> tasks = [...];

    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> updated)
    {
        tasks = updated.ToList();
    }
}
```
